caption: Cleaning up before uninstall
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes/uninstall-cleanup
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

TiddlyWiki has no plugin-uninstall hook, so state tiddlers under
`$:/state/json-convert/...` persist after the plugins are removed.  These
are the Console's pasted source and chosen profile, and the editor's
working state — small and inert, but if you want a clean uninstall:

```
<$button>
Clean up json-convert state
<$list filter="[prefix[$:/state/json-convert/]]" variable="t">
<$action-deletetiddler $tiddler=<<t>>/>
</$list>
</$button>
```

Paste that into a new tiddler, click the button, then uninstall the
plugins — the Studio first, then the runtime.  Everything a ''Convert''
produces (staged tiddlers, decisions, results, the session log) lives
under `$:/temp/...`, which is session-only and needs no cleanup.
